{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr]_f \\ar[rd]_p & &\nY \\ar[dl]^q \\\\\n& B\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$q$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "SPACE_0004": "\\ ", "SPACE_0005": "\\ ", "SPACE_0006": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-syntomic-smooth-etale-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6e8e7b91757f581539739603920b47b15b10d39acb62af4b19f2340d658fe76b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c0199c8e30e2d3ddfa6a3048f3c4d8fa0ff53a3746830d2b346745c73a52377f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe a commutative diagram of morphisms of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nAssume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is surjective, and syntomic (resp.<SPACE_0001>smooth, resp.<SPACE_0002><ACCENT_0001>tale),\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is syntomic (resp.<SPACE_0003>smooth, resp.<SPACE_0004><ACCENT_0002>tale).\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen <MATH_0006> is syntomic (resp.<SPACE_0005>smooth, resp.<SPACE_0006><ACCENT_0003>tale).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b7b3fcce90dd00d1a017177bdbe505cc8225e858d956c6cf474a602f8320507", "unit_id": "tag:0AHD:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$|X| \\to |Y|$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-syntomic-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-smooth-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-local}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{descent-lemma-syntomic-smooth-etale-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87578af789e2474d524ffeea733a380801e777372c9e51b5449ddd2143052682", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7a674731f5979de4d0cb23b7483f9660e537f79339bed6f926062764ded2c353", "source_text": "We deduce this from the analogue for schemes.\nNamely, the problem is <ACCENT_0001>tale local on <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas\n<REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>).\nHence we may assume that <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are affine\nschemes. Since <MATH_0005> is open\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0004>),\nwe can choose an affine\nscheme <MATH_0006> and an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism <MATH_0007> such that the\ncomposition <MATH_0008> is surjective. In this case the result\nfollows from Descent, Lemma\n<REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3fff1e547463def41cce5bb48ce8362c8a5ed57234671530bed0923e7621c9aa", "unit_id": "tag:0AHD:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6f490743f7550ed4df3028ff79916b3a3023c2eb67ce4345a22d5f78fd9ee5a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nActually we can strengthen this result as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:73cbb7e9369aaffccab5598048792598bfa601497d1eed5b6139e36e6daed8a8", "unit_id": "tag:06NQ:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr]_f \\ar[rd]_p & &\nY \\ar[dl]^q \\\\\n& B\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$q$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-smooth-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6e8e7b91757f581539739603920b47b15b10d39acb62af4b19f2340d658fe76b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3e82644437905d0be1e04f5c77bcf53b79c9e8e7e6b6ac4b0000daa63c5d6c2c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe a commutative diagram of morphisms of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is smooth (resp.<SPACE_0001><ACCENT_0001>tale).\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen <MATH_0006> is smooth (resp.<SPACE_0002><ACCENT_0002>tale).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:73639110cc7420dcf480491765b6c9ca39277b7446d65edcc304cd6141fe4b30", "unit_id": "tag:0AHE:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$|X| \\to |Y|$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-smooth-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{descent-lemma-smooth-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87578af789e2474d524ffeea733a380801e777372c9e51b5449ddd2143052682", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:547610accec26c3fe5c6d8ef0d4b26061d868dc575a9c37c33616037298e08a1", "source_text": "We deduce this from the analogue for schemes.\nNamely, the problem is <ACCENT_0001>tale local on <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas\n<REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>).\nHence we may assume that <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are affine\nschemes. Since <MATH_0005> is open\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0003>),\nwe can choose an affine\nscheme <MATH_0006> and an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism <MATH_0007> such that the\ncomposition <MATH_0008> is surjective. In this case the result\nfollows from Descent, Lemma\n<REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:14412f6bddd39f66caa1c1ebeda5ce09be479ecf6d3f69b146620e66bb81240b", "unit_id": "tag:0AHE:proof"}
